# Counter
A button that counts its clicks:  the smallest app there is.
The Counter notebook, `@spell/notebooks/Counter`, draws its own and tries it out.

## A counter
Each counter is its own element on the page.

<spell-view "counter">
	<property "count" type="number" description="How many times it's been clicked:  a new counter starts at 0">0</property>
	<action "count up">set the count to the count + 1</>

	<draw description="A button saying how many times it's been clicked:  a click counts up">
		<button onClick={count up}>Clicked {the count} times</button>
	</draw>

	<test "counting">
		set the counter to a new counter
		the counter's count should be 0
		count up of the counter
		count up of the counter
		the counter's count should be 2
	</test>
</spell-view>

## The app:  one counter, drawn

<spell-app "counter app">
	<property "counter">a new counter</>
	<draw>
		<container>{draw the counter}</container>
	</draw>
</spell-app>
